# W Linux — PAM stack for hyprlock (screen lock).
#
# hyprlock only authenticates (no session/account/password phases), so a single
# auth include is all it needs. Delegating to system-auth means the lock accepts
# the same password as login (pam_unix). This guarantees password unlock always
# works regardless of what the hyprlock package ships as its default.
#
# Fingerprint unlock is NOT wired through PAM here: hyprlock talks to fprintd
# directly over D-Bus (auth:fingerprint in hyprlock.conf), in parallel with this
# password path. See package-hyprlock.md.
auth include system-auth
